[LCNT.4.1] The language must not grow any of the following:

- `for each`, loops, cursors, or iterators over a grouping's contents;
- list, array, or map types whose purpose is sequential traversal;
- comprehensions, or `map` / `filter` / `reduce` taking an
  author-written lambda;
- any operation whose cost is data-dependent and unbounded.

Each is a collection surface by [LCNT.1.2], and [LCNT.1.3] forecloses
it. The last also fails the bounded-cost requirement independently
([LCNT.5.2]).
